# 🔐 Lab 1 – Identity & Access Management in Azure

## 📌 Overview

This lab demonstrates the implementation of **identity and access management controls** in Microsoft Azure using a least-privilege model. The objective was to configure secure access using RBAC, enforce MFA, 
implement Privileged Identity Management (PIM), and apply Azure Policy to prevent insecure configurations.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

* Implement **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** with least privilege
* Configure **Privileged Identity Management (PIM)** for just-in-time access
* Enforce **Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)** using Conditional Access
* Enable **diagnostic logging and monitoring**
* Deploy **Azure Policy** to enforce security baselines
* Map implementations to compliance frameworks

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

Identity and access were structured using:

* Azure AD users and groups
* Role assignments at the subscription level
* Conditional Access enforcing MFA
* Azure Policy preventing insecure configurations

---

